{"base_rate":0.08661417322834646,"brier":0.04658228346456693,"bss":0.4111867946708465,"bss_hi":0.5459921623778085,"bss_lo":0.2588472181659157,"country":"US","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.03408136482939633,"ess":263.77998209804656,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Los Angeles</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Los Angeles rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (48%), believe about\n<b>64%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nLOS ANGELES 2.6 NW, 4.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.41, ranked 30 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(7&ndash;74) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>584</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>101</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 3 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Los Angeles</b> <span class=\"muted\">US</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.41</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>7&ndash;74\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Los Angeles &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Los Angeles\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 68.76019801980198,356.7722772277228 227.92,174.0 227.92,240.1818181818182 68.76019801980198,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"350.4724409448819\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"350.4724409448819\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,377.63698630136986 68.76019801980198,345.96039603960395 227.92,150.36363636363637\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 584 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"377.63698630136986\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 101 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"68.76019801980198\" cy=\"345.96039603960395\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 48%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"227.92\" cy=\"150.36363636363637\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(9%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Los Angeles the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.56) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.05).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'>0.049</td><td class='num'>0.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'>0.267</td><td class='num'>6.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'>0.413</td><td class='num'>3.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'>0.564</td><td class='num'>4.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":34.05223,"lon":-118.24368,"n":762,"n_cities":109,"name":"Los Angeles","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":584,"obs":0.011986301369863013,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1389999999999998,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.030396039603960395,"n":101,"obs":0.09900990099009901,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.1389999999999998,"mean":0.4799999999999999,"n":77,"obs":0.6363636363636364,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.2,"rank":30,"rank_hi":74.02499999999998,"rank_lo":7.0,"reliability":0.0032047458672088782,"resolution":0.034828459144668436,"slug":"los-angeles","station":"LOS ANGELES 2.6 NW","timezone":"America/Los_Angeles"}